WEBVTT

00:11.762 --> 00:13.639
I wanted to run away
from the pawn shop.

00:14.765 --> 00:18.267
But there was a shadow of misfortune
that fell on my shoulders.

00:18.268 --> 00:21.688
It was a weight
that I just couldn't shake off.

00:35.869 --> 00:38.538
Do you know
how worried I've been?

00:38.539 --> 00:40.206
You've got a perfectly good home.

00:40.207 --> 00:41.666
Why are you putting yourself through this?

00:41.667 --> 00:44.544
Oh, no! Mm!

00:44.545 --> 00:46.295
Look at you.
Your poor hands.

00:46.296 --> 00:49.132
Whatever. Can you just go now?

00:51.927 --> 00:53.469
'Kay, I'll go.

00:53.470 --> 00:55.430
But you should
come home more often.

00:56.390 --> 00:58.850
We can all have dinner together, yeah?

01:07.401 --> 01:09.444
Gross. That bastard.

01:14.324 --> 01:18.704
I swore to myself I would never
be lured by that light that got my mother.

01:19.871 --> 01:21.998
I needed a light of my own.

01:21.999 --> 01:23.792
One that would hide me from my shadow.

01:25.127 --> 01:28.589
But without money,
you don't have a lot of options.

01:32.843 --> 01:35.928
Gold Land makes promises
of dazzling fortune.

01:35.929 --> 01:37.764
But that's not what I dreamed of.

01:39.016 --> 01:44.479
Maybe all I wanted was just some guarantee
that I could be safe here.

01:45.397 --> 01:47.440
It was all someone like me could hope for.

01:57.075 --> 01:58.326
Hey, hey, hey, hey.

01:58.327 --> 02:01.162
- What's the deal with these red ones?
-  Sorry?

02:01.163 --> 02:03.623
They're all supposed to be yellow.
I exchanged them for yellow!

02:05.375 --> 02:06.376
Ch-change it!

02:07.794 --> 02:09.712
Hey! Hear me or what?

02:09.713 --> 02:11.505
-  All right, that's enough.
- Do you think I'm stupid, bitch?

02:11.506 --> 02:13.799
-  Time to go, sir.
-  Let's go.

02:13.800 --> 02:15.801
Let go of me!
Get your hands off me!

02:15.802 --> 02:19.055
- Call the manager! Call the manager now!
-  Get him out. Let's go!

02:19.056 --> 02:20.307
What the hell?

02:20.974 --> 02:22.142
What's up with that guy?

02:26.438 --> 02:28.522
Oh.

02:28.523 --> 02:30.776
100 gold chips, please.

02:32.069 --> 02:34.654
That's when he walked
into my life.

02:34.655 --> 02:38.449
A man who seemed to be made
of nothing but good luck.

02:38.450 --> 02:42.036
He was like a mirage
that came out of nowhere.

02:42.037 --> 02:43.705
Something that didn't belong in my world.

02:44.623 --> 02:46.792
As if he'd disappear if I touched him.

02:48.126 --> 02:51.672
Time to see if luck is on
my side today.

02:53.965 --> 02:55.300
Thank you, Miss Heeju.
:cue

03:05.018 --> 03:07.354
I bought this on my way back
from Hong Kong. It's for you.

03:08.355 --> 03:09.898
Heard you like planes, so...

03:13.110 --> 03:16.738
Uh, 100 gold chips, please.

03:34.714 --> 03:37.801
Time to see if luck is on my side today.

03:41.346 --> 03:42.556
Thank you.

03:53.483 --> 03:54.984
Whew!

04:01.950 --> 04:02.950
Yes!

04:09.332 --> 04:10.749
Did you see that?

04:15.797 --> 04:19.301
Hey, see this?
It's yours Heeju.

04:20.427 --> 04:22.136
I only won it because of you.

04:32.939 --> 04:33.940
Uh...

04:49.247 --> 04:52.334
Give me some gold chips,
why don't ya?

04:54.628 --> 04:57.464
This is where you were hiding, huh?

04:58.507 --> 05:00.967
Do you have any idea
how long I've been looking for you?

05:03.553 --> 05:05.179
Get out.

05:05.180 --> 05:07.223
I don't have anything to say to you.

05:07.224 --> 05:08.933
That's no way to talk to your uncle.

05:08.934 --> 05:12.770
Like it or not,
the two of us are family, ya know.

05:12.771 --> 05:14.272
You are not my family.

05:15.398 --> 05:17.400
Hmm.

05:18.151 --> 05:20.195
But you're my sweet little niece.

05:22.781 --> 05:25.908
Enough of this.
Let's just go home now.

05:25.909 --> 05:28.619
Did my aunt tell you, then?
Where to find me?

05:28.620 --> 05:29.620
Of course.

05:29.621 --> 05:31.205
She was worried sick.

05:31.206 --> 05:33.332
You're her only niece.

05:33.333 --> 05:36.168
Come back home now, really.
Heeju.

05:36.169 --> 05:38.087
-  Do you really think...
- Security, he's drunk.

05:38.088 --> 05:41.465
...you can live in Jeongsan
without me finding out about it?

05:41.466 --> 05:42.591
-  Let's go, let's go.
-  Come on.

05:42.592 --> 05:45.219
I'm this girl's uncle, okay?

05:45.220 --> 05:48.556
Ah, shitheads!
Get the hell off of me!

05:48.557 --> 05:50.266
She's my niece!
I'm telling you!

05:50.267 --> 05:52.018
-  Come on!
- Be sure to eat well, okay?

05:52.936 --> 05:55.437
-  You've lost weight, you know!
-  Even the light of this place

05:55.438 --> 05:57.690
- couldn't conceal my shadow.
-  I'll be back for you! Heeju!
:cue

05:57.691 --> 06:04.155
HAENGBOK PAWNSHOP

06:04.781 --> 06:06.867
How much longer could I endure?

06:08.076 --> 06:09.661
Like my mother...

06:10.662 --> 06:12.414
...I was already starting to wither.

06:14.791 --> 06:16.960
I felt like I couldn't go on much longer.

06:18.003 --> 06:19.462
I had to reach for it.

06:20.797 --> 06:23.883
Even if it was just
a mirage that would disappear.

06:56.374 --> 06:57.375
Heeju.

07:06.551 --> 07:07.552
Here you go.

07:08.553 --> 07:10.972
I exchanged those chips you gave me
into cash for you.

07:14.100 --> 07:17.979
Uh, I'm sorry.
I didn't mean it that way.

07:19.147 --> 07:20.481
What did you mean, then?

07:20.482 --> 07:25.445
Well, either way it was up to you
to decide whether to come here or not.

07:28.281 --> 07:30.407
But take this at least.

07:30.408 --> 07:32.661
As a token of my appreciation.

07:37.999 --> 07:39.875
This is everything I have.

07:39.876 --> 07:43.213
Take the money and place
a single bet for me.

07:44.339 --> 07:46.173
I've decided to trust you.

07:46.174 --> 07:47.676
And for once in my life...

07:48.385 --> 07:51.513
...take a gamble and see if my life
has any luck at all.

07:54.974 --> 07:58.686
The game at table two
will start in one minute.

07:58.687 --> 08:00.438
You have one minute
if you want to play.

08:04.567 --> 08:05.984
Congrats, Heeju.
Good job.

08:05.985 --> 08:08.571
You won.
The pot is all yours.

08:13.410 --> 08:15.077
Wait a sec, Heeju.

08:15.078 --> 08:16.287
Just a sec.

08:18.123 --> 08:20.374
It's okay.

08:20.375 --> 08:23.210
-  It's okay.
-  Wait. I don't...

08:23.211 --> 08:25.212
Let's place these ones on top.

08:25.213 --> 08:26.548
What?

08:28.717 --> 08:30.343
Trust me, Heeju.

09:03.168 --> 09:04.335
Ten.

09:08.715 --> 09:10.216
Okay.

09:16.514 --> 09:18.807
Heeju! Heeju, you did it!

09:18.808 --> 09:20.643
You won it all!

09:22.353 --> 09:24.480
Okay, these are yours.

09:25.982 --> 09:27.608
This is enough, right?

09:27.609 --> 09:28.943
Congratulations.

09:30.445 --> 09:34.323
From then on,
for the first time in my life,

09:34.324 --> 09:36.993
it finally felt like there
was a light in my world.

09:38.369 --> 09:40.496
Like I was seeing the sun
for the first time

09:40.497 --> 09:42.457
after coming out of a dark tunnel.

09:43.333 --> 09:48.045
It was warm and everything around me
was crystal clear.

09:48.046 --> 09:49.088
- Come here.
- What?

09:49.089 --> 09:52.800
Every moment,
every day filled with gratitude.

09:52.801 --> 09:54.260
I was happy.

09:55.678 --> 09:58.222
What, you don't like mine?
What's not to like?

09:58.223 --> 10:01.684
:cue

10:08.608 --> 10:09.609
What are you staring at?

10:13.404 --> 10:16.365
Am I really allowed
to live like this?

10:16.366 --> 10:17.492
What does that mean?

10:19.494 --> 10:20.870
Just like this.

10:22.831 --> 10:24.165
Like other people.

10:25.375 --> 10:26.751
Happy and calm.

10:29.671 --> 10:31.840
You met me,
so you must be lucky.

10:34.759 --> 10:37.345
You're the first person
to ever say that to me.

10:38.596 --> 10:40.180
Ever since I was a kid,

10:40.181 --> 10:43.017
everyone always told me I
was an unlucky little brat.

10:44.394 --> 10:45.645
And it was kind of true.

10:46.729 --> 10:48.648
So none of this feels real.

10:49.607 --> 10:51.359
Being happy like this.

10:53.570 --> 10:54.695
Being with you.

10:58.616 --> 11:00.200
Isn't happiness meant for everyone?

11:00.201 --> 11:01.202
Mm.

11:02.245 --> 11:04.414
You don't have
to worry about anything now.

11:05.331 --> 11:06.875
Just trust me and follow my lead.

11:07.709 --> 11:09.334
This is barely the beginning.

11:09.335 --> 11:11.254
From this moment on...

11:12.380 --> 11:16.134
...I'm gonna show you exactly
how lucky you are.

11:18.803 --> 11:19.804
Santé?

11:23.975 --> 11:24.975
Santé.

11:44.913 --> 11:50.919
NO ENTRY

12:45.181 --> 12:46.474
Is this mine?

12:48.017 --> 12:49.018
No.

12:50.228 --> 12:52.105
Then is it Lee Dokyung's?

12:53.481 --> 12:54.857
Also no.

12:56.609 --> 12:58.069
I don't know whose it is.

12:59.195 --> 13:01.406
Maybe I don't wanna know.

13:02.323 --> 13:04.700
But if it doesn't belong
to anyone anyway,

13:04.701 --> 13:05.702
why shouldn't I take it?

13:07.537 --> 13:09.622
At least,
that's what I kept telling myself.

13:11.165 --> 13:13.209
You're just doing what Lee Dokyung
told you to do.

13:14.127 --> 13:15.962
You can't help it because you love him.

13:16.671 --> 13:18.006
That's what you think, right?

13:19.215 --> 13:21.842
Did I really love Lee Dokyung?

13:21.843 --> 13:24.804
Or was it that I just wanted to escape?

13:26.347 --> 13:27.890
Did it really matter?

13:30.351 --> 13:36.024
No, but now I have
to decide for myself.

13:36.774 --> 13:39.944
What does it really mean to be happy?

14:05.553 --> 14:08.556
:cue

14:27.366 --> 14:28.992
EPISODE 4
HIM

14:28.993 --> 14:31.412
Stop bugging me about it, okay?

14:31.954 --> 14:33.205
I'll find it soon.

14:34.540 --> 14:36.541
Yes, I know that.

14:36.542 --> 14:38.668
The chairman will be back next week?

14:38.669 --> 14:40.546
I'll get back
to you as soon as I can.

14:41.255 --> 14:42.422
Yeah.

14:43.758 --> 14:45.842
Oh! Ah!

14:45.843 --> 14:47.844
Ah, fuck me.

14:47.845 --> 14:49.221
Seriously?

15:00.149 --> 15:02.401
Ah, shit.

15:06.906 --> 15:08.366
Is that a woman?

15:27.468 --> 15:30.388
WITNESS STATEMENT RECORD
WITNESS PERSONAL INFORMATION

15:37.311 --> 15:38.729
And your name?

15:40.565 --> 15:41.941
Yeo Sunok.

15:46.195 --> 15:47.780
Around what time
did this happen?

15:50.700 --> 15:51.784
Um...

15:52.702 --> 15:55.495
Last night.
Around 10:00.

15:55.496 --> 15:57.497
Okay, around 10:00 p.m.

15:57.498 --> 15:58.707
Afternoon, sir.

15:58.708 --> 15:59.959
- Wait!
- Yeah?

16:00.543 --> 16:02.085
Well, that woman.

16:02.086 --> 16:03.920
What's her deal?

16:03.921 --> 16:04.963
Ah, her?

16:04.964 --> 16:06.548
She was booked this morning
at a local precinct,

16:06.549 --> 16:07.632
but they handed it over to us.

16:07.633 --> 16:10.510
She bashed her husband with a golf club.
He's in the hospital.

16:10.511 --> 16:11.887
Her husband reported it?

16:11.888 --> 16:14.347
No, she reported it herself.

16:14.348 --> 16:15.682
What about the husband?

16:15.683 --> 16:17.058
He wants to press charges.

16:17.059 --> 16:20.312
According to him, she-
she was after his pawnshop's money.

16:20.313 --> 16:23.190
- Says he has evidence.
-  Sunok!

16:23.191 --> 16:26.526
Sunok! What's going on here?
Is it true?

16:26.527 --> 16:28.570
Well, I'll be going.

16:28.571 --> 16:30.614
- You didn't really do it, did you?
- Hi, there.

16:30.615 --> 16:32.073
Are you a family member?

16:32.074 --> 16:34.409
No, but she's like a sister.

16:34.410 --> 16:35.702
How did you find out?

16:35.703 --> 16:36.870
What are you saying?

16:36.871 --> 16:39.040
You called me to come and get you.

16:41.334 --> 16:43.251
Can you make sure she leaves?

16:43.252 --> 16:45.295
Sunok, dammit,
that's not what should concern you.

16:45.296 --> 16:46.881
You shouldn't be here.

16:48.049 --> 16:50.258
Detective, this woman
is very sick.

16:50.259 --> 16:52.303
She has terminal cancer.

16:54.472 --> 16:57.140
I mean, she should be in
the hospital, not in a place like this!

16:57.141 --> 16:59.477
I understand, but I
still have to continue processing her.

17:00.394 --> 17:02.479
- Detective, please!
- Jeongsan-gun.

17:02.480 --> 17:05.440
- Sunok!
- Five, dash, 18 Bukju.

17:05.441 --> 17:06.858
Detective!

17:06.859 --> 17:09.862
SAMJEON JEWELRY DEPARTMENT STORE

17:10.821 --> 17:13.324
Ah, okay.
No, no, no, no.

17:14.116 --> 17:15.284
Excuse me.

17:17.745 --> 17:19.329
Yeah, sure thing.

17:19.330 --> 17:20.665
Thank you. Mm.

17:22.625 --> 17:26.378
We could have made preparations
if you had called ahead of time.

17:26.379 --> 17:27.421
Sorry about that.

17:30.007 --> 17:32.342
But we'll buy the gold bar.
We'll have the cash ready soon.

17:32.343 --> 17:33.468
Do you mind waiting
a little longer?

17:33.469 --> 17:34.427
Of course.

17:43.521 --> 17:45.856
Uh, sir. Excuse me.

17:46.983 --> 17:49.484
This one here.
Can I buy this?

17:49.485 --> 17:51.611
Uh, would you like to look
at that one, too?

17:51.612 --> 17:53.614
- Heh, yeah.
- Sure. Just one minute.

18:00.871 --> 18:02.163
You want it in cash?

18:02.164 --> 18:03.957
130 million?

18:03.958 --> 18:05.250
Yeah.

18:06.794 --> 18:08.253
If you can't do it, don't worry.

18:08.254 --> 18:09.671
- I'll go somewhere else.
- Oh, no, no, no, no.

18:09.672 --> 18:12.133
Wait just a minute.

18:16.304 --> 18:18.555
Honey, I want this one!

18:18.556 --> 18:20.515
- Isn't it beautiful?
- Really?

18:20.516 --> 18:22.225
You don't want this one?
It's shiny.

18:22.226 --> 18:23.810
Happy with that little thing?

18:35.114 --> 18:36.448
You don't want to count to make sure?

18:36.449 --> 18:39.826
I plan on doing more business with you,
so I'm sure it's the right amount.

18:39.827 --> 18:41.369
Ah, yes.

18:42.496 --> 18:44.914
KIM MINCHEOL

18:44.915 --> 18:46.666
RESIDENT REGISTRATION CARD
KIM MINCHEOL
:cue

18:46.667 --> 18:48.418
JEWELRY WORLD

18:50.254 --> 18:52.130
Heeju, what's up?

18:52.131 --> 18:53.132
Where are you?

18:54.050 --> 18:55.593
Where do you think? Daejeong.

18:56.510 --> 18:58.262
Just finishing up with the potatoes.

18:58.721 --> 18:59.804
Where are you?

18:59.805 --> 19:01.057
You don't need to know.

19:02.350 --> 19:04.643
I need you to just show me where you
are right now.

19:04.644 --> 19:06.979
Ah, why can't you just trust me?

19:09.231 --> 19:11.233
See? Jewelry stores.

19:12.610 --> 19:13.693
By the way,

19:13.694 --> 19:15.071
I think I'm gonna get a new car.

19:15.905 --> 19:17.782
I'm young and rich now.

19:18.699 --> 19:20.493
This car doesn't cut it anymore.

19:23.371 --> 19:26.665
Well anyway,
I'll be headed over there later.

19:26.666 --> 19:29.585
You just, uh, bring the gold.

19:30.211 --> 19:31.253
See you soon.

19:56.237 --> 20:00.074
YANGPO INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT

20:40.865 --> 20:41.948
And who are you?

20:41.949 --> 20:45.744
Oh, uh, hi.
Jeongsan Police Department.

20:45.745 --> 20:48.705
Uh, Detective Kim Jinman.

20:48.706 --> 20:51.207
Here's my business card for you.

20:51.208 --> 20:53.001
The Jeongsan Police?

20:53.002 --> 20:55.795
I thought that my team was cleared
of any involvement

20:55.796 --> 20:57.422
and the investigation was over.

20:57.423 --> 20:59.382
Yeah, sort of.

20:59.383 --> 21:01.926
This particular case has become so complex

21:01.927 --> 21:04.220
that we're conducting
a joint investigation.

21:04.221 --> 21:06.514
And regarding Mr. Lee Dokyung,

21:06.515 --> 21:07.933
we haven't caught the suspect
for the hit-and-run.

21:09.810 --> 21:12.437
So the police still haven't been able
to find the casket?

21:12.438 --> 21:15.273
- No, not yet.
-  Hmm.

21:15.274 --> 21:16.859
What do you want to ask me about, exactly?

21:17.985 --> 21:19.360
You're close with Lee Dokyung, right?

21:19.361 --> 21:20.613
You two call each other a lot?

21:21.697 --> 21:23.032
Because of work, I guess.

21:23.616 --> 21:25.867
There's nothing going on between us.

21:27.536 --> 21:29.288
It's been a while since we've talked.

21:30.456 --> 21:31.749
So what's going on?

21:34.001 --> 21:36.211
I don't really know,
but I might need a favor.

21:37.963 --> 21:40.215
Could you get something through customs
for me?

21:40.216 --> 21:42.259
Favor?

21:43.636 --> 21:44.969
Why?

21:44.970 --> 21:47.014
Why not just tell me you love me
like you used to?

21:48.224 --> 21:49.767
You can't say it anymore?

21:51.644 --> 21:53.938
You said it just fine
when you were cheating on me.

21:54.605 --> 21:57.690
This is important.
I'm not playing around here.

21:57.691 --> 22:00.528
You spoke with him on the phone
on the day of the accident, the fourth.

22:02.696 --> 22:05.573
Was I the only person who spoke
to Lee Dokyung that day?

22:05.574 --> 22:06.658
Not at all.

22:06.659 --> 22:08.743
Miss, this is just standard procedure.

22:08.744 --> 22:09.954
I have to ask, 'kay?

22:11.121 --> 22:12.705
Lee Dokyung, what did he say?

22:13.916 --> 22:15.792
THIS IS THE LAST TIME.
PLEASE JUST COME ONE MORE TIME TOMORROW.

22:15.793 --> 22:17.795
I CAN GIVE YOU WHAT YOU REALLY WANT.
NATIONAL ROUTE 6, 50-7

22:20.589 --> 22:22.466
We just talked
about personal stuff.

22:23.717 --> 22:26.010
But I don't really feel like getting
into all that right now.

22:26.011 --> 22:27.388
Oh.

22:28.556 --> 22:32.100
So you're close enough to speak
about personal matters on the phone. Mm.

22:32.101 --> 22:34.395
The day of the accident, then.

22:34.979 --> 22:37.356
Do you happen to know anyone who
could verify where you were?

22:38.274 --> 22:39.482
My alibi?

22:39.483 --> 22:41.150
Your alibi, yeah.

22:41.151 --> 22:42.652
You've already gone through
my call history.
:cue

22:42.653 --> 22:44.237
Shouldn't you already know?

22:44.238 --> 22:45.947
You see, the thing is,

22:45.948 --> 22:49.325
we can't verify anything you did after
the call with Lee Dokyung.

22:49.326 --> 22:52.495
At 10:00 p.m., you turned your phone off
for the rest of the night.

22:52.496 --> 22:55.415
Well, I would have been home
at that time.

22:55.416 --> 22:56.500
Mm-hmm.

22:57.626 --> 23:00.587
Ah, wait.
I went to the theater that night.

23:00.588 --> 23:02.463
For a late night movie.

23:02.464 --> 23:04.841
Movie theater?
Which theater did you go to?

23:04.842 --> 23:06.134
The theater in Sokcho.

23:06.135 --> 23:08.596
Alone or with someone?

23:09.513 --> 23:11.973
- I went alone.
-  I see.

23:14.435 --> 23:18.146
Do you happen to have anything that you
can show me like a ticket stub

23:18.147 --> 23:20.482
or reservation E-mail that shows you
were there that night?

23:21.442 --> 23:22.776
I'll be sure to look for it.

23:23.319 --> 23:25.321
Yes, please do.
I'd appreciate that.

23:26.947 --> 23:28.157
You know what?

23:30.159 --> 23:31.159
Whenever I question a suspect,

23:31.160 --> 23:34.787
the most common alibi
is that they were at the theater.

23:34.788 --> 23:36.581
If you had told me you were at home,

23:36.582 --> 23:39.293
I could have confirmed with
the surveillance cameras pretty easily.

23:39.752 --> 23:41.754
Unfortunately, the movie theaters
are trickier.

23:43.213 --> 23:45.299
Did you drive to the theater?

23:46.216 --> 23:48.176
- Well, no.
-  Ah.

23:48.177 --> 23:49.969
It's not a big deal.
It's honestly nothing.

23:49.970 --> 23:52.931
Just wait for my call and then bring
a van to the location I tell you.

23:52.932 --> 23:54.058
That's all.

23:54.892 --> 23:55.975
No.

23:57.436 --> 23:58.895
Get out.

23:58.896 --> 24:00.146
Do it yourself.

24:00.147 --> 24:01.648
Don't even think about involving me.

24:01.649 --> 24:03.399
It's a billion.

24:03.400 --> 24:04.859
Is this what you meant
by giving me what I wanted?

24:04.860 --> 24:06.653
Yujin! Are you listening?

24:06.654 --> 24:08.696
Not a million.
It's a billion won.

24:08.697 --> 24:10.698
Don't you think that amount
is worth betting on?

24:10.699 --> 24:11.908
Betting?

24:11.909 --> 24:14.453
Your whole life is just one big gamble.

24:15.245 --> 24:16.579
No.

24:16.580 --> 24:19.791
It just never ends with you.
There will always be more.

24:19.792 --> 24:21.794
You'll keep doing this until it kills you.

24:23.003 --> 24:24.922
But you don't get to ruin my life,
too, so get out.

24:25.798 --> 24:28.758
Yujin, we're so close. You can't-

24:28.759 --> 24:30.511
don't-don't tell me
you're bailing out now!

24:32.888 --> 24:34.722
Dokyung, this isn't fun anymore.

24:34.723 --> 24:37.309
- What?
-  Get out.

24:38.978 --> 24:40.354
I said go.

24:52.700 --> 24:55.368
- Am I a suspect?
-  Oh, no, no, no, no, no.

24:55.369 --> 24:59.247
I'm just saying, it's quite a coincidence,
the whole theater thing. Yeah.

24:59.248 --> 25:00.624
I get it, though.

25:03.836 --> 25:05.004
Hmm.

25:06.171 --> 25:08.631
So what's going to happen
to Lee Dokyung after all this?

25:08.632 --> 25:13.052
Ah, well, he'll be transferred
to a detention center upon recovery

25:13.053 --> 25:15.680
and then depending on
the outcome of his trial,

25:15.681 --> 25:18.599
I'd say he'll likely serve
a year or two in prison.

25:18.600 --> 25:21.060
I thought you told me you hadn't found
the casket yet.

25:21.061 --> 25:24.564
If there's no evidence,
will he still go to jail?

25:24.565 --> 25:26.941
No, but I'm sure we'll find
the casket soon. Yeah.

25:26.942 --> 25:27.943
Oh.

25:29.570 --> 25:30.653
Well, then,

25:30.654 --> 25:32.948
I think that's just about everything
I wanted to ask you.

25:34.283 --> 25:37.285
That means I need to speak
with Kim Heeju next.

25:37.286 --> 25:42.040
So are you able to call her here for me,
or do I go somewhere else?

25:42.041 --> 25:44.042
- Kim Heeju?
- Yeah.

25:44.043 --> 25:48.129
Kim Heeju's alibi
hasn't been confirmed yet?

25:48.130 --> 25:49.964
No, we haven't been able
to get a hold of her,

25:49.965 --> 25:51.759
so her alibi is still unclear.

25:52.718 --> 25:54.428
Heeju resigned recently.

25:55.554 --> 25:58.514
She resigned? Why?

25:58.515 --> 26:00.601
She said it was personal.

26:01.518 --> 26:02.519
Oh.

26:04.146 --> 26:05.354
Really?

26:05.355 --> 26:06.647
TEAM LEADER
CHA YUJIN

26:06.648 --> 26:10.068
If you can't reach her, I'll give her
a call and tell her to contact you, okay?

26:10.069 --> 26:12.488
Ah, yeah, if you could do that,
I'd appreciate it.

26:13.572 --> 26:15.449
Apologies for barging in earlier.

26:16.241 --> 26:17.242
Yeah.

26:18.327 --> 26:19.869
Did you buy that yourself?

26:19.870 --> 26:21.038
No, it was a gift.

26:21.622 --> 26:22.623
Gotcha.

26:23.540 --> 26:26.585
Again, apologies for earlier.
Yeah.
:cue

26:38.013 --> 26:39.597
What's going on with belt two?

26:39.598 --> 26:42.976
It's all the metal decorations
attached to the casket.

26:43.936 --> 26:44.937
Let it go through.

27:06.667 --> 27:10.170
He's gonna ask where you were
when Lee Dokyung had his accident.

27:11.130 --> 27:12.131
Come up with an alibi.

27:22.057 --> 27:23.891
Heeju!

27:44.913 --> 27:46.956
You bought a car?

27:46.957 --> 27:49.584
I bought a new car.
Like it?

27:49.585 --> 27:52.295
The sound is insane.
It's fucking surround sound!

27:56.133 --> 27:59.969
Heeju, you should buy a car or something, too.

28:02.806 --> 28:05.308
We already paid the goldsmith one potato.

28:05.309 --> 28:07.977
And I took four out of the 12
as my share.

28:07.978 --> 28:09.562
And that's the rest.

28:09.563 --> 28:13.066
800 million.

28:14.818 --> 28:16.320
We really did it.

28:17.279 --> 28:18.280
I told you.

28:19.281 --> 28:22.575
Heeju, have you ever seen so much cash?

28:22.576 --> 28:24.452
Couldn't even imagine it!

28:24.453 --> 28:25.828
It's crazy!

28:25.829 --> 28:27.496
We're loaded now!

28:31.543 --> 28:35.171
That's one potato down.
Time for us to dig up the next one.

28:52.397 --> 28:54.565
Oh, Cheoljung, it's me.

28:54.566 --> 28:57.360
How's your head feeling?
Are you okay?

28:57.361 --> 29:00.071
I can't believe Sunok lost
her temper like that.

29:00.072 --> 29:01.365
Let me see.

29:02.491 --> 29:04.200
Good thing it isn't worse, right?

29:04.201 --> 29:07.578
Sunok came back
to her senses after she hurt you.

29:07.579 --> 29:09.581
She called the police
and turned herself in.

29:10.248 --> 29:12.208
I told you,
Sunok didn't do it.

29:12.209 --> 29:13.542
What do you mean?

29:13.543 --> 29:16.045
She already told me everything.

29:18.298 --> 29:19.633
You'll drop the charges, right?

29:21.093 --> 29:23.011
You wouldn't really send her
to jail, would you?

29:25.180 --> 29:27.348
You know she has cancer.

29:27.349 --> 29:28.641
She needs a hospital.

29:28.642 --> 29:30.977
She wouldn't make it in a cold jail cell.
:cue

29:30.978 --> 29:33.229
I beg you.
She is your wife.

29:35.357 --> 29:36.566
My wife?

29:37.609 --> 29:39.777
That bitch was stealing my money.

29:39.778 --> 29:42.154
And I doubt she'd care
if I was killed.

29:44.282 --> 29:50.621
About that. Uh, she said she's planning
on returning it all to you.

29:50.622 --> 29:52.123
So if it's about the money,
don't worry bec-

29:52.124 --> 29:53.332
Who said?

29:53.333 --> 29:55.669
Who else? Sunok!

29:56.837 --> 29:58.422
It's Heeju, huh?

30:00.257 --> 30:01.883
Ah, no.

30:02.801 --> 30:05.136
Why would you-Sunok, of course.

30:05.137 --> 30:07.514
She said she hasn't spent any
of the money yet.

30:08.223 --> 30:10.683
I haven't seen Heeju in over five years.

30:10.684 --> 30:13.436
Why are you suddenly asking about her?

30:13.437 --> 30:16.857
Tell Heeju to bring
the money to me herself.

30:18.025 --> 30:19.026
Got it?

30:21.945 --> 30:24.948
Or I'll throw her in
the slammer with her aunt.

30:37.252 --> 30:39.920
Heeju!
This is bad. We're fucked.

30:39.921 --> 30:41.797
That bastard must have seen you.

30:41.798 --> 30:44.091
He says you have to bring him
the money yourself

30:44.092 --> 30:45.509
or he'll report you to the police!

30:45.510 --> 30:47.511
You mean that asshole's still alive?

30:47.512 --> 30:48.971
Yes, he's still alive!

30:48.972 --> 30:51.766
He got a few stitches but he survived
and now the bastard's awake.

30:51.767 --> 30:54.101
And apparently he's filing
a police report.

30:54.102 --> 30:55.561
I tried to convince him it wasn't you.

30:55.562 --> 30:57.272
- I really tried.
-  It's fine, Auntie.

30:58.607 --> 31:00.649
-  I'll take care of it.
- What are you gonna do?

31:00.650 --> 31:02.318
Are you gonna go in there
and meet him face-to-face?

31:02.319 --> 31:03.819
Or are you gonna turn yourself in
to the police?

31:03.820 --> 31:06.906
Oh, it's not like your life
isn't fucked up enough already.

31:06.907 --> 31:11.160
Honestly, why is everyone
so hell-bent on screwing themselves over?

31:11.161 --> 31:12.162
Shit!

31:19.044 --> 31:21.213
What happened? Something wrong?

31:22.089 --> 31:24.007
Who's the asshole?

31:29.679 --> 31:31.430
Heeju.

31:31.431 --> 31:32.932
We're partners now, aren't we?

31:32.933 --> 31:35.351
Huh? We're supposed to talk to each other.

31:35.352 --> 31:37.145
Your business is my business.

31:39.606 --> 31:41.191
Do you actually believe that?

31:42.776 --> 31:43.944
That my business is yours?

31:44.820 --> 31:46.947
Of course.
Think about it.

31:48.323 --> 31:53.119
If somethin' happens to you,
it'll screw up our business, hmm?

31:53.120 --> 31:56.580
We only sold one potato.
There's plenty more to do.

31:56.581 --> 31:57.749
I need you for that.

32:13.723 --> 32:15.558
How come you won't just tell me?

32:15.559 --> 32:17.310
I mean, who is it?

32:21.815 --> 32:22.983
You gonna answer?
:cue

33:54.950 --> 33:56.701
Shit.

33:59.204 --> 34:01.372
Pretty damn thorough.

34:01.373 --> 34:02.373
NO DATA

34:02.374 --> 34:03.583
She erased everything.

34:06.044 --> 34:09.797
JEIL WORKSHOP

34:29.192 --> 34:32.946
So, uh,
about the situation with your uncle.

34:34.114 --> 34:35.323
I thought about what you told me.

34:37.075 --> 34:38.158
Two options here.

34:38.159 --> 34:42.454
First, give the bastard more money
than he asked for.

34:42.455 --> 34:45.416
Then make him sign something
saying he'll never tell anyone.

34:45.417 --> 34:46.876
Well, that's the first option, anyway.

34:51.631 --> 34:53.216
What's the second option?

34:56.928 --> 34:59.763
I mean, I don't think you'll like it even
if I tell you,

34:59.764 --> 35:01.683
because you're, like,
conscientious and all.

35:02.559 --> 35:03.602
:cue

35:08.857 --> 35:10.774
Don't worry.

35:10.775 --> 35:12.610
You wouldn't have to do it yourself.

35:12.611 --> 35:15.697
I'll do it for you.
And I'll clean it up, too.

35:19.242 --> 35:20.994
Have you killed people before?

35:23.079 --> 35:24.122
Well, I mean...

35:25.457 --> 35:28.418
...for money, yeah.
I'll do anything for money.

35:29.586 --> 35:30.753
For how much?

35:32.505 --> 35:35.466
Well, a one-kilo gold bar.

35:38.887 --> 35:41.847
What about my aunt?
Is she trapped in jail?

35:41.848 --> 35:45.602
I mean, if we-
if we get rid of him, then...

35:46.895 --> 35:48.854
...she'd be released
'cause there's no real case.

35:48.855 --> 35:49.981
Oh, wait.

35:50.523 --> 35:52.358
Maybe she'd still have
to serve a year or two.

35:55.695 --> 35:57.112
How about this one?

35:57.113 --> 35:58.448
This batch turned out great.

35:59.616 --> 36:01.492
The bars are super smooth.

36:01.493 --> 36:03.410
Nice and shiny.

36:04.829 --> 36:06.872
Looks like you're getting better
and better each time.

36:10.251 --> 36:11.335
Okay, back to work.

36:11.336 --> 36:12.462
We're talking here.

36:13.380 --> 36:14.381
Ah.

36:25.558 --> 36:27.060
The first option is good.

36:30.814 --> 36:33.315
Option one, then.
Not my money.

36:52.252 --> 36:54.545
JINGOGAE THREE-WAY INTERSECTION

36:58.341 --> 36:59.676
Looks like she was lying.

37:01.052 --> 37:02.053
Just watching a movie?

37:03.346 --> 37:05.640
Now I got you, lady.

37:08.935 --> 37:10.269
CHA YUJIN

37:15.442 --> 37:17.651
-  Gyeongsu.
- Yeah?

37:17.652 --> 37:18.819
I'm exhausted.

37:18.820 --> 37:20.696
Well you've been working hard.

37:20.697 --> 37:23.450
Oh, yeah.
That woman who hit her husband.

37:24.534 --> 37:25.659
Was it attempted murder?

37:25.660 --> 37:27.369
- Oh, Yeo Sunok?
-  Yeah.

37:27.370 --> 37:29.037
Where's she at?

37:29.038 --> 37:30.372
She's in the holding cell.

37:30.373 --> 37:31.915
Why?

37:31.916 --> 37:34.668
What's up with you?
Why are you still working so late?

37:34.669 --> 37:36.713
The-the report isn't done yet.

37:38.173 --> 37:39.298
Get back to it.

37:39.299 --> 37:40.592
Yeah.
:cue

37:47.599 --> 37:50.017
-  Sir.
-  Yeah.

37:50.018 --> 37:53.687
Listen, I have a few questions
for the detainee.

37:53.688 --> 37:56.024
Do you mind giving me the room just
for ten minutes?

37:57.150 --> 37:58.400
Of course, sir.

38:05.784 --> 38:06.785
Thanks.

38:09.412 --> 38:10.996
- Come back in 10.
-  Yes, sir.

38:10.997 --> 38:12.749
'Kay.

38:39.734 --> 38:40.735
Hey.

38:41.694 --> 38:44.655
Of all the places we could have met, huh?

39:02.715 --> 39:04.843
Did you beat your husband
with a golf club?

39:05.510 --> 39:07.803
Mm-hmm.

39:07.804 --> 39:09.305
Why?

39:10.682 --> 39:12.433
Just wanted the bastard dead.

39:13.643 --> 39:16.937
Ah, that temper of yours.

39:16.938 --> 39:20.191
If you say things like that in court,
they'll put you right in prison.

39:21.109 --> 39:22.443
I don't care.

39:23.611 --> 39:24.904
So what if they do?

39:26.239 --> 39:28.449
It wouldn't even make that much
of a difference.

39:29.450 --> 39:32.160
Your husband says it was 'cause of money.

39:33.496 --> 39:34.914
Well, that's part of it, too.

39:41.546 --> 39:43.797
So this morning I overheard something.

39:43.798 --> 39:46.759
You have cancer?
That true?

39:47.927 --> 39:50.095
Seems like it.

39:50.096 --> 39:51.764
Then stop smoking, Sunok.

39:52.932 --> 39:54.349
Uh, here.

40:04.152 --> 40:05.486
You mean to settle?

40:06.487 --> 40:08.406
No, I'll just go to prison, I think.

40:09.741 --> 40:11.283
It sounds easier.

40:16.623 --> 40:18.958
I'll go talk to your husband in
a couple of days.

40:19.959 --> 40:21.002
Don't bother.

40:21.711 --> 40:23.171
It doesn't matter.

40:45.735 --> 40:48.195
If you order a drink then shut up
and fucking drink it

40:48.196 --> 40:49.905
- like a good little boy. You hear that?
- Oh, fuck you!

41:02.251 --> 41:05.087
GWIBIN COFFEE SHOP

41:05.088 --> 41:06.798
The police, police!

41:07.757 --> 41:09.758
We're the police!
Break it up!

41:09.759 --> 41:10.968
Hey, hey!

41:10.969 --> 41:12.094
Don't push me!

41:12.095 --> 41:15.055
Come on!
That's enough. That's enough.

41:15.056 --> 41:16.098
Hey, hey.

41:16.099 --> 41:17.516
Just calm down.

41:17.517 --> 41:19.601
-  Hey!
-  Leave her alone.

41:22.188 --> 41:23.564
- Put me down!
-  There he goes!

41:33.992 --> 41:35.201
Give me a light?

41:43.084 --> 41:44.627
:cue

41:48.798 --> 41:50.675
How come your hands are so pretty?

41:52.468 --> 41:53.969
You play piano, officer?

41:53.970 --> 41:55.054
Uh, no, ma'am.

42:04.355 --> 42:05.356
Guess it's true.

42:06.691 --> 42:08.233
Men in uniform are pretty sexy.

42:50.485 --> 42:51.778
Heeju!

42:52.612 --> 42:53.696
You're here.

42:54.447 --> 42:56.866
I was wondering when you'd show up.

43:00.828 --> 43:02.121
Just look at you!

43:03.664 --> 43:05.583
All grown up.
A real woman now.

43:06.793 --> 43:11.129
I'm only here-I'm here to-
to return the money Auntie took from you.

43:11.130 --> 43:13.382
What she stole?

43:14.383 --> 43:15.384
Sure.

43:16.302 --> 43:18.471
How much money?

43:19.972 --> 43:21.224
100 million.

43:26.979 --> 43:29.524
And how are you planning on returning it?

43:30.233 --> 43:32.317
I can send it
to your bank account.

43:32.318 --> 43:34.904
Or if you want I can give it
to you in cash.

43:36.030 --> 43:37.739
Really?

43:37.740 --> 43:39.492
Hmm.

43:40.368 --> 43:42.452
Well, I want it back in cash.

43:42.453 --> 43:43.829
Yes.

43:43.830 --> 43:45.456
But before that...

43:46.499 --> 43:48.876
...you have to drop
the charges against auntie.

43:50.711 --> 43:52.796
Sure, no problem.

43:52.797 --> 43:54.923
Then the three of us can live together.

43:54.924 --> 43:57.300
We're family after all, aren't we?

43:57.301 --> 43:58.386
No.

44:01.472 --> 44:03.182
Auntie isn't doing very well.

44:04.267 --> 44:05.268
It's cancer.

44:06.060 --> 44:07.603
She might not live long.

44:09.272 --> 44:10.982
So I want her to get treated.

44:11.607 --> 44:13.316
In a hospital.

44:13.317 --> 44:16.945
While there's still time
and she can live comfortably.

44:16.946 --> 44:18.865
I'll stay by her side
while she's there.

44:19.448 --> 44:20.658
But uncle...

44:21.617 --> 44:23.911
...you're going to leave town
and not come back.

44:25.913 --> 44:27.707
Why would I?

44:29.083 --> 44:30.625
See, the thing is,

44:30.626 --> 44:33.003
the house and the shop are here,
so where would I go?

44:33.004 --> 44:34.589
You can sell the pawnshop to me.

44:36.215 --> 44:37.883
I've already looked into it.

44:37.884 --> 44:41.761
I know all about the loans and that
the shop is being used as collateral.

44:41.762 --> 44:44.932
I'll take over your debts,
pay you the rest...

44:45.766 --> 44:47.226
...and I'll even pay in cash.

44:48.644 --> 44:49.854
How much?

44:51.689 --> 44:53.733
How much do you want for it?

44:56.360 --> 45:00.031
I won't sell it at market price. Hm.

45:01.282 --> 45:03.742
Maybe for a billion won,
I'd let you have it.

45:03.743 --> 45:05.244
Okay.

45:08.206 --> 45:09.706
Seriously?

45:09.707 --> 45:12.543
You got that kinda cash?
That much?

45:14.629 --> 45:15.630
Yeah.

45:16.839 --> 45:17.924
Is that so?

45:18.883 --> 45:20.968
For that kind of money...

45:21.886 --> 45:23.971
Come to the pawnshop
by 10:00 o'clock tonight.

45:25.014 --> 45:27.140
I'll have the contract
and the money ready for you.

45:27.141 --> 45:28.142
But first...

45:29.810 --> 45:31.437
...you need to drop the charges.

45:32.230 --> 45:33.481
Or the deal's off.

45:34.398 --> 45:35.566
Mm-hmm.

45:36.525 --> 45:37.568
Okay.
:cue

45:59.465 --> 46:00.882
How did it go?

46:00.883 --> 46:03.468
One billion to take his debt
and the store.

46:03.469 --> 46:05.179
Ah, shit, that's crazy.

46:06.222 --> 46:09.933
A billion won for that crumbling,
one-story building? Really?

46:09.934 --> 46:12.186
- Drop me off at Yangpo Airport.
-  Why?

46:12.895 --> 46:14.896
I'm a bit short on cash.

46:14.897 --> 46:16.107
How much more do you need?

46:16.857 --> 46:19.276
I can have it ready
for you in just two days.

46:19.277 --> 46:23.238
No, it has to be today.
I want to get my aunt out quickly.

46:24.740 --> 46:26.659
We're fucked. Shit.

46:28.494 --> 46:30.913
Let me just lend it to you, okay?

46:34.583 --> 46:36.042
CONFIRMATION OF SEVERANCE PAY RECEIPT
KIM HEEJU

46:39.297 --> 46:42.049
We will now
begin boarding.

46:46.053 --> 46:48.680
I'll tell them to send it out immediately,
since it seems urgent.

46:48.681 --> 46:51.224
Oh, thank you very much.
I appreciate it, Ms. Cha.

46:51.225 --> 46:53.393
Where are you living nowadays, Heeju?

46:53.394 --> 46:54.312
What?

46:55.229 --> 46:57.605
I decided to take a look at your resume.

46:57.606 --> 47:00.192
Your address and listed family are fake.

47:01.944 --> 47:03.654
What exactly are you hiding?

47:05.698 --> 47:08.325
- I'm staying with my aunt.
-  Oh, really?

47:08.326 --> 47:10.286
And where does your aunt live?

47:11.329 --> 47:12.371
In Jeongsan.

47:13.205 --> 47:14.540
Jeongsan?

47:15.124 --> 47:18.710
Have you been to Jeongsan,
by any chance, recently?

47:18.711 --> 47:20.587
- No.
-  Okay.

47:20.588 --> 47:22.297
You haven't then.

47:22.298 --> 47:24.133
Why are you asking?

47:24.633 --> 47:26.468
Seems the smuggling
accomplice went

47:26.469 --> 47:28.596
to Jeongsan with the casket.

47:32.933 --> 47:34.143
There's no way.

47:35.186 --> 47:36.979
You're the accomplice.

47:37.980 --> 47:39.065
What?

47:39.940 --> 47:41.733
Have you given your alibi?

47:41.734 --> 47:44.652
Uh, no, not yet.

47:44.653 --> 47:45.654
Okay, well...

47:46.864 --> 47:49.532
...give the detective a call.
Do that first.

47:49.533 --> 47:51.409
It might be best
to get ahead of it.

47:51.410 --> 47:54.412
Just don't mention you're in Jeongsan,
because the thing is,

47:54.413 --> 47:56.956
the police know that the van carrying
the casket went there.

47:56.957 --> 47:59.667
Heeju, they're gonna find you.

47:59.668 --> 48:01.087
It's only a matter of time.

48:04.090 --> 48:07.425
I'm not sure I know
what you're talking about.

48:10.096 --> 48:11.138
Okay.

48:12.223 --> 48:14.724
Can't blame you, I guess.

48:14.725 --> 48:15.893
Lee Dokyung is a bad guy.

48:17.144 --> 48:18.603
Didn't I ever tell you?

48:18.604 --> 48:19.605
No?

48:20.731 --> 48:22.942
Lee Dokyung and I dated for a while.

48:24.235 --> 48:25.444
Not anymore, though.

48:26.904 --> 48:29.240
I was on National Route 6 that day, too.

48:29.990 --> 48:32.951
He asked me to help him move the casket.

48:32.952 --> 48:35.537
Obviously, I refused to help out.

48:35.538 --> 48:37.456
You were clearly too blinded
by love, though.

48:38.416 --> 48:39.417
It made you foolish.

48:40.918 --> 48:44.421
He has as lover
in every location he flies to
:cue

48:44.422 --> 48:46.214
I bet you didn't know that.

48:46.215 --> 48:50.094
China, Hong Kong, Vietnam, Japan.

48:52.179 --> 48:54.181
There are probably more here, too,
that we don't know about.

48:55.474 --> 48:58.060
Do you think he actually loves
all those women?

48:59.228 --> 49:00.395
Or are you telling yourself,

49:00.396 --> 49:05.568
those relationships are all fake,
and you're the only one he truly loves?

49:10.823 --> 49:14.577
I seriously don't know what you mean
by any of these things.

49:16.996 --> 49:18.998
Ms. Cha, why are you telling me all this?

49:19.915 --> 49:20.958
I'm trying to help you.

49:22.168 --> 49:24.586
We're suspects.

49:24.587 --> 49:27.089
As long as you're in the clear,
then I'm in the clear.

49:28.257 --> 49:32.595
Lee Dokyung is just using you
and you keep letting him.

49:33.929 --> 49:35.097
He's not worth it.

49:36.390 --> 49:38.808
I wish you had just run off
with the casket yourself.

49:38.809 --> 49:40.144
That would have been better.

49:41.228 --> 49:44.355
But could you really hold out
on your own with the casket,

49:44.356 --> 49:46.025
until Lee Dokyung gets outta jail?

49:52.490 --> 49:53.949
Remember this, Heeju.

49:54.909 --> 49:56.951
I'm the only person on your side now.

49:56.952 --> 50:00.788
If something happens,
you should call me immediately.

50:00.789 --> 50:02.082
I can help you out.

50:38.452 --> 50:40.871
What? Are they not gonna pay you?

50:41.914 --> 50:43.665
Want me to take care of it?

50:43.666 --> 50:45.000
No.

50:53.050 --> 50:54.175
THIS IS DETECTIVE KIM JINMAN.
PLEASE CALL ME WHEN YOU SEE THIS MESSAGE.

50:54.176 --> 50:55.177
I'M CONTACTING YOU FOR A WITNESS
INTERVIEW. I HAVE A FEW THINGS TO ASK YOU.

50:56.220 --> 50:58.221
- Ah, shit.
-  What?

50:58.222 --> 51:00.265
Who is it?

51:00.266 --> 51:02.351
It's the police.

51:03.269 --> 51:04.270
What?

51:05.187 --> 51:06.188
What do they want?

51:07.231 --> 51:09.649
Shit, did that fucker
Han Cheoljung report you?

51:09.650 --> 51:12.610
No, the detective looking for the casket.

51:12.611 --> 51:15.656
He suspects I helped Lee Dokyung.

51:16.657 --> 51:19.952
Sounds like the police also know that
the van went to Jeongsan that day.

51:25.583 --> 51:27.709
Ah, shit.

51:27.710 --> 51:29.627
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.
Hold on.

51:29.628 --> 51:30.629
What are you doing?

51:31.589 --> 51:33.882
If I don't call him,
he'll suspect me more.

51:37.052 --> 51:38.137
Hold on a sec.
:cue

51:46.895 --> 51:48.396
Put it on speaker, okay?

51:52.484 --> 51:54.777
This is Detective Kim Jinman

51:54.778 --> 51:55.988
- of the Jeongsan Police.
- Uh...

51:56.530 --> 51:57.614
...yes, hello.

51:57.615 --> 52:00.617
You called because I used
to work at Yango Airport?

52:00.618 --> 52:02.160
- This is Kim Heeju.
- Kim Jinman of Jeongsan?

52:02.161 --> 52:04.370
Oh, yeah. Yeah, yeah.

52:04.371 --> 52:07.957
Seems like Cha Yujin finally managed
to get a hold of you, then.

52:07.958 --> 52:10.793
Anyway, well, I tried calling a bunch.

52:10.794 --> 52:13.588
Then I stopped by your house
but you weren't there either.

52:13.589 --> 52:17.885
I even went to Yangpo Airport
and they told me you left the company.

52:19.303 --> 52:20.928
Is that right?
You no longer work there?

52:20.929 --> 52:26.894
Uh, yeah, I've just been busy
with personal stuff so...

52:27.978 --> 52:29.730
No worries.
Nothing major.

52:30.731 --> 52:32.566
Just need to know where you were the day
of Lee Dokyung's accident.

52:34.360 --> 52:36.737
The date was September fourth,
if you recall.

52:38.447 --> 52:41.533
Uh, after I got off work...

52:42.660 --> 52:47.580
...I remember I drove up to-
to Gangneung for the evening.

52:47.581 --> 52:50.124
Gangneung?
And why go there?

52:50.125 --> 52:51.877
You came all the way back
to work the next day.

52:52.920 --> 52:57.507
Yeah, I just wanted
to clear my head,

52:57.508 --> 52:59.801
so I went shopping
and then went to see a movie.

52:59.802 --> 53:01.178
JEONGSAN POLICE STATION (INVESTIGATIONS
DIVISION) DETECTIVE KIM JINMAN

53:03.013 --> 53:05.974
A movie, huh? On your own?

53:08.060 --> 53:09.352
Yeah.

53:09.353 --> 53:10.895
I see.

53:10.896 --> 53:12.272
You don't have a car, right?

53:13.065 --> 53:14.273
No.

53:14.274 --> 53:15.650
Okay, I got it.

53:15.651 --> 53:16.984
JEONGSAN POLICE STATION (INVESTIGATIONS
DIVISION) DETECTIVE KIM JINMAN

53:16.985 --> 53:18.236
I'll be able to check
the rest on my end here.

53:18.237 --> 53:20.280
All right, well,
thanks for calling.

53:21.323 --> 53:22.490
Ooh.

53:22.491 --> 53:24.075
Ah, shit!

53:24.076 --> 53:26.119
Kim Jinman's with the company.

53:26.120 --> 53:29.330
- He's a detective.
- Yeah, well, obviously.

53:29.331 --> 53:31.083
But he's a detective who works with us.

53:33.627 --> 53:35.504
Hey, Detective.
Doing okay?

53:37.464 --> 53:39.675
Jeongsan Police,
Investigations Division, right?

53:40.592 --> 53:43.386
That means it's not the fucking cops.
It's Yes Money chasing you.

53:43.387 --> 53:44.888
They want to find their casket.

53:46.265 --> 53:48.851
Ah, we're really fucked now.

53:53.105 --> 53:54.355
- Oh.
- Sir.

53:54.356 --> 53:56.024
Uh, looks like the charges
are being dropped.

53:56.525 --> 53:58.401
- O-open it. I need to talk to her.
- Yes, sir.

53:58.402 --> 53:59.318
Thanks.

54:02.114 --> 54:03.865
Ms. Yeo Sunok.

54:05.242 --> 54:06.535
Yeo Sunok.

54:07.411 --> 54:09.663
What? Miss Yeo Sunok.

54:11.039 --> 54:13.751
Hey, Yeo Sunok.

54:15.836 --> 54:18.254
Sunok. Sunok! Wake up!

54:18.255 --> 54:19.881
Hey, help me out here!

54:19.882 --> 54:21.132
Yes, sir.

54:22.593 --> 54:24.010
Okay, call 911.

54:24.011 --> 54:26.095
- Call them right now!
-  Yes, sir.

54:43.822 --> 54:45.699
Sunok. Sunok, wake up.
Come on.

54:47.784 --> 54:49.495
What's wrong with her?

54:50.120 --> 54:51.913
Doc-doctor!

54:51.914 --> 54:53.831
No!

54:53.832 --> 54:55.125
Sunok, no!

54:55.751 --> 54:58.294
Sunok, please, open your eyes!

54:58.295 --> 54:59.629
Sunok!

54:59.630 --> 55:01.172
Please!

55:04.384 --> 55:07.136
They said she got blood
in her lungs and went into shock.

55:07.137 --> 55:08.554
Oh, so stupid.

55:08.555 --> 55:11.307
She could have asked them
to take her to the hospital.

55:11.308 --> 55:14.727
But instead she just sat there suffering
with a hole in her lung.

55:14.728 --> 55:16.146
Like she wanted to die.

55:17.064 --> 55:18.899
So, what did you say to your uncle?

55:19.733 --> 55:22.443
He dropped the charges.
How did you manage that?

55:24.029 --> 55:26.948
Will you please do me a favor
and stay with her tonight?

55:26.949 --> 55:27.907
I'll be there tomorrow.

55:31.286 --> 55:33.789
Tonight? It's Friday, though.

55:34.373 --> 55:37.543
I'm supposed to be working tonight.

55:40.003 --> 55:42.923
I-I'll pay you a million won
for your trouble.

55:44.424 --> 55:45.925
Okay, okay.

55:45.926 --> 55:47.761
I'm sorry, auntie.
Thank you.

55:55.686 --> 55:56.687
Heeju.

56:01.733 --> 56:03.150
Let's take a sec to think about it.

56:03.151 --> 56:04.319
About what?

56:06.196 --> 56:09.115
About shutting Han Cheoljung up
with hush money.

56:09.116 --> 56:10.158
How can you be sure?

56:10.993 --> 56:12.786
That asshole could still
rat you out after.

56:14.830 --> 56:16.330
The second he gives your name
to the police,

56:16.331 --> 56:17.874
Detective Kim will find out, too.

56:18.750 --> 56:21.128
That means he'll know without
a doubt you went to Jeongsan.

56:25.090 --> 56:27.508
But he did get my aunt out
like he promised.

56:27.509 --> 56:28.635
Exactly.

56:29.553 --> 56:31.471
So you don't have
to worry about her anymore.
:cue

56:40.522 --> 56:42.065
Didn't you say you wanted him dead?

56:43.859 --> 56:44.942
Heeju.

56:44.943 --> 56:46.695
You think it'll end here?

56:47.154 --> 56:48.279
Not a chance.

56:48.280 --> 56:50.656
I know assholes
like him too damn well.

56:50.657 --> 56:53.535
He'll keep coming back,
asking for money again and again.

56:57.372 --> 56:59.790
As long as you and your aunt
are still here,

56:59.791 --> 57:00.876
he'll never leave you alone.

57:02.210 --> 57:05.171
Why put yourself in such
a dangerous situation?

57:05.172 --> 57:06.965
And if Detective Kim catches you...

57:08.050 --> 57:09.842
...then it'll all be over, Heeju.

57:09.843 --> 57:11.720
The gold bars.
Everything.

57:13.305 --> 57:20.312
HAENGBOK PAWNSHOP

57:34.660 --> 57:36.995
Haengbok Pawnshop, huh?

57:43.126 --> 57:44.628
Heeju!

57:58.975 --> 58:00.060
Read it over.

58:13.657 --> 58:16.075
So, the money.
Where is it?

58:16.076 --> 58:18.411
I wanna see it myself first.

58:40.183 --> 58:43.061
I didn't believe you!
What the...

58:43.603 --> 58:46.480
...what the hell have you been doing
all these years, Heeju?

58:46.481 --> 58:50.193
I mean, how could you
possibly have this kind of money?

58:54.531 --> 58:55.781
Sign the contract.

58:55.782 --> 58:58.118
Uh, okay.
Yeah, sure.

59:07.461 --> 59:09.796
You know I can't do it, Heeju.

59:13.341 --> 59:16.594
Let's stop
and think this over again, okay?

59:16.595 --> 59:19.221
Who cares
who owns the pawnshop?

59:19.222 --> 59:20.390
That doesn't matter.

59:21.308 --> 59:23.142
Family is all that matters.

59:23.143 --> 59:26.813
You and me, your aunt,
we should all live together.

59:29.149 --> 59:30.608
Sign the contract.

59:30.609 --> 59:32.569
I'm not telling you again.

59:32.986 --> 59:35.029
The whole drive here,

59:35.030 --> 59:36.948
I put a lotta thought into this.

59:39.201 --> 59:40.409
Your poor aunt.

59:40.410 --> 59:43.537
She has cancer
and not much time to live.

59:43.538 --> 59:46.832
I just think while she's alive,
she'd be happier if we were all together.

59:46.833 --> 59:48.375
We're supposed to be family.

59:52.964 --> 59:55.090
- Family?
-  If we weren't family,

59:55.091 --> 59:58.093
I would've reported you
to the police right away, ya know?

59:58.094 --> 01:00:00.763
You swung that club at me.

01:00:00.764 --> 01:00:03.266
I saw your face as clear as day.

01:00:04.643 --> 01:00:08.687
Or would you rather I go
to the police right now

01:00:08.688 --> 01:00:10.982
and let 'em know it was you?

01:00:15.987 --> 01:00:19.073
What should I spend all this money on?
Pay off the loan?

01:00:19.074 --> 01:00:22.201
Well, seeing as it is our store,
let's do that.

01:00:22.202 --> 01:00:25.622
Oh, sweetie, being on your own
was so hard wasn't it?

01:00:32.045 --> 01:00:35.214
No. No! No! No!

01:00:35.215 --> 01:00:37.132
Ah, shit.

01:00:42.639 --> 01:00:44.473
Ah, you little shit.

01:00:50.856 --> 01:00:52.940
Don't even think
about leaving.

01:00:52.941 --> 01:00:56.151
Just stay here
and look after the pawnshop.

01:00:56.152 --> 01:01:00.197
While your aunt dies.

01:01:14.546 --> 01:01:15.547
Goodbye.

01:01:20.594 --> 01:01:21.970
Woogy!

01:01:28.643 --> 01:01:31.145
Bastard, who are you?

01:01:34.190 --> 01:01:36.735
Evil son of a bitch.
:cue

01:01:42.574 --> 01:01:44.199
Should I do it?

01:01:50.999 --> 01:01:52.000
Yeah.

01:01:54.794 --> 01:01:55.879
Do it.
